#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:0
msgid ""
"Reference documentation for environment variables available to snap "
"applications, including paths, data directories, revisions, libraries, and "
"desktop support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:8
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:10
msgid ""
"Environment variables are widely used across Linux to provide convenient "
"access to system and application properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:12
msgid ""
"Both Snapcraft and snapd consume, set, and pass-through specific environment "
"variables to support building and running snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:14
msgid ""
"See below for the various environment variables available to snap "
"applications. For environment variables connected to Snapcraft, see [Parts "
"environment variables](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/"
"reference/part-environment-variables/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:16
msgid "List environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:18
msgid ""
"Each snap runs in a custom environment specifically made for it. To get an "
"overview of the variables in it, you can open a shell as the snap and run "
"the `env` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:20
msgid ""
"$ snap run --shell <snap>.<command>\n"
"$ env\n"
"XDG_VTNR=1\n"
"SSH_AGENT_PID=5543\n"
"XDG_SESSION_ID=2\n"
"SNAP_USER_COMMON=/home/<user>/snap/<snap>/common\n"
"SNAP_LIBRARY_PATH=/var/lib/snapd/lib/gl:\n"
"SNAP_COMMON=/var/snap/<snap>/common\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""

