#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:37
msgid ""
"Directory where the snap is mounted. This is where all the files in your "
"snap are visible in the filesystem. All of the data in the snap is read-only "
"and cannot be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:40
msgid "Typical value: `/snap/hello-world/27`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:42
msgid "<pre>SNAP_USER_DATA</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:44
msgid "Directory for user data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:46
msgid ""
"This directory is backed up and restored across `snap refresh` and `snap "
"revert` operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:48
msgid "Typical value: `/home/zyga/snap/hello-world/27`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:50
msgid "The final number there is `$SNAP_REVISION`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:52
msgid "<pre>SNAP_USER_COMMON</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:54
msgid "Directory for user data that is common across revisions of a snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:56
msgid ""
"Unlike `SNAP_USER_DATA`, data present in this directory is not backed up or "
"restored across `snap refresh` and `snap revert` operations. The directory "
"is suitable for large data that the application can access even if it was "
"made or modified by a future version of a snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:58
msgid "Typical value `/home/zyga/snap/hello-world/common`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:60
msgid "<pre>SNAP_DATA</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:62
msgid "Directory for system data of a snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:64
msgid ""
"This directory is owned and writable by `root` and is meant to be used by "
"background applications (daemons, services). Unlike `SNAP_COMMON` this "
"directory is backed up and restored across `snap refresh` and `snap revert` "
"operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:66
msgid "Typical value `/var/snap/hello-world/27`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:68
msgid "<pre>SNAP_COMMON</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:70
msgid "Directory for system data that is common across revisions of a snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:72
msgid ""
"This directory is owned and writable by `root` and is meant to be used by "
"background applications (daemons, services). Unlike `SNAP_DATA` this "
"directory **is not** backed up and restored across snap refresh and revert "
"operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:74
msgid "Typical value: `/var/snap/hello-world/common`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:76
msgid "<pre>SNAP_SAVE_DATA</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:78
msgid ""
"**This variable is only exposed on {ref}`Ubuntu Core <ref-glossary_ubuntu-"
"core>` systems.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:80
msgid ""
"It points to a snap-specific location on the ubuntu-save partition where the "
"snap is allowed to store persistent files (like certificates or "
"configuration files) that will survive a [factory reset](https://"
"documentation.ubuntu.com/core/explanation/recovery-modes/#factory-reset) of "
"the Ubuntu Core device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:82
msgid ""
"See [ubuntu-save](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/explanation/core-"
"elements/storage-layout/#the-ubuntu-save-partition) in the Ubuntu Core "
"documentation for more details on storage layout with this specific "
"partition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:84
msgid "Requires _snapd_ 2.57+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:86
msgid "<pre>SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:88
msgid "The name of snap instance, including instance key if one is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:90
msgid ""
"For example snap `hello-world` with instance key `foo` has instance name "
"equal to `hello-world_foo`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:92
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:110
msgid "Typical value: `hello-world`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:94
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:104
msgid "Requires _snapd_ 2.36+"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:96
msgid "<pre>SNAP_INSTANCE_KEY</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:98
msgid "Instance key if one was set during installation or empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:100
msgid "For example instance `hello-world_foo` has an instance key `foo`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:102
msgid "Typical value: none"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:106
msgid "<pre>SNAP_NAME</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:108
msgid "The name of the snap as specified in the `snapcraft.yaml` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:112
msgid "<pre>SNAP_REVISION</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:114
msgid ""
"Revision of the snap, as allocated by the Snap Store on upload or as "
"allocated by snapd for locally installed snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:116
msgid ""
"The Snap Store assigns monotonic revisions to each upload of a given snap. "
"Snapd uses Snap Store revisions if accompanying assertions are available or "
"uses a locally generated number. Locally generated numbers are prefixed with "
"`x` to distinguish them from Snap Store uploads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:118
msgid "Typical value: `27` or `x1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:120
msgid "<PRE>SNAP_ARCH</PRE>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:120
msgid "<PRE>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:120
msgid "</PRE>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:122
msgid "CPU architecture of the running system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:124
msgid "Typical value `amd64`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:126
msgid "Other values are: `i386`, `armhf`, `arm64`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:128
msgid "<pre>SNAP_UID</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:130
msgid ""
"This variable contains the user ID (uid) of the user running this snap "
"instance. See also SNAP_EUID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:132
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:144
msgid ""
"For this variable to be exposed by a snap, the snap developer will need to "
"include the following `assumes` value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:134
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:146
msgid "assumes: [snap-uid-envvars]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:138
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:150
msgid "Requires _snapd_ 2.59+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:140
msgid "<pre>SNAP_EUID</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:142
msgid ""
"This variable contains the _effective_ user ID (euid) of the user running "
"the snap instance. See also SNAP_UID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:152
msgid "<pre>SNAP_LAUNCHER_ARCH_TRIPLET</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:154
msgid ""
"**Only available in snaps built with a [desktop extension](https://"
"documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/reference/extensions).**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:156
msgid ""
"The host architecture triplet on which the snap is running. For `amd64` it's "
"`x86_64-linux-gnu`. The runtime counterpart of "
"`CRAFT_ARCH_TRIPLET_BUILD_FOR`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:158
msgid "<pre>SNAP_LIBRARY_PATH</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:160
msgid ""
"Directory with additional system libraries. This variable is used internally "
"by snapcraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:162
msgid ""
"The value is always `/var/lib/snapd/lib/gl:` Please note the colon at the "
"end of that value, the variable is a colon-separated list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:164
msgid ""
"The referenced directory is typically empty unless Nvidia proprietary "
"drivers are in use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:166
msgid "<pre>SNAP_VERSION</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:168
msgid "The version string as specified in the `snapcraft.yaml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:170
msgid "Typical value `6.3`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:172
msgid "<pre>SNAP_REAL_HOME</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:174
msgid ""
"The vanilla `HOME` environment variable before snapd-induced remapping, "
"refer to [Any way to acquire the originally set `HOME` environment variable? "
"- snapcraft - snapcraft.io](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/any-way-to-acquire-"
"the-originally-set-home-environment-variable/19475) for more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:176
msgid "Requires _snapd_ 2.46+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:178
msgid "<pre>SNAP_APP_NAME</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:180
msgid ""
"The name of the application being run, as specified in the `snapcraft.yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:182
msgid "Only set when running an application command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:184
msgid "Typical value: `my-snap-app`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:186
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:196
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:208
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:218
msgid "Requires _snapd_ 2.77+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:188
msgid "<pre>SNAP_APP_COMMON_ID</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:190
msgid ""
"The common identifier of the application, as specified by the `common-id` "
"field in `snapcraft.yaml`. This is typically a reverse-DNS identifier used "
"to associate the application with its desktop entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:192
msgid "Only set when running an application that defines a `common-id`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:194
#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:216
msgid "Typical value: `org.example.Foo`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:198
msgid "<pre>SNAP_APP_DESKTOP_FILE</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:200
msgid "The absolute path to the application's installed desktop file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:202
msgid ""
"Only set when running an application that has an associated desktop file on "
"disk. The value depends on the use of the `common-id` property, or the "
"`desktop-file-ids` attribute in the `desktop` interface plug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:204
msgid "Typical values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:205
msgid "`/var/lib/snapd/desktop/applications/my-snap-name_my-snap-app.desktop`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:206
msgid "`/var/lib/snapd/desktop/applications/org.example.Foo.desktop`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:210
msgid "<pre>SNAP_APP_BUS_NAME</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:212
msgid ""
"The D-Bus bus name the application is allowed to own, as specified by the "
"`bus-name` field in `snapcraft.yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:214
msgid "Only set when running an application that defines a `bus-name`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:220
msgid "<pre>SNAP_COMPONENTS</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:222
msgid ""
"Path to components directory. Installed components are available under "
"`$SNAP_COMPONENTS/<comp-name>/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:225
msgid "Typical value: /snap/hello-world/components/27"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:227
msgid "Requires _snapd_ 2.78+"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:229
msgid "Generic variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:231
msgid "<pre>HOME</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:233
msgid ""
"For non-classic snaps, this environment variable is re-written to "
"`SNAP_USER_DATA` by snapd so that each snap appears to have a dedicated home "
"directory that is a subdirectory of the real home directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:235
msgid "For classic confinement snaps, the value remains unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:237
msgid ""
"Typical value: `/home/_user_name_/snap/_snap_name_/_snap_revision_` (e.g. `/"
"home/zyga/snap/hello-world/27`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:239
msgid "<pre>PATH</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:241
msgid ""
"This environment variable is re-written by snapd so that it is consistent "
"with the view of the filesystem presented to snap applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:243
msgid "The value is always:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:245
msgid "For non-classic confinement snaps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:247
msgid ""
"$SNAP/usr/sbin:$SNAP/usr/bin:$SNAP/sbin:$SNAP/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/"
"bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/games:/usr/local/games\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/environment-variables.md:249
msgid ""
"For classic confinement snaps:       `/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/"
"sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/games:/usr/local/games`"
msgstr ""

